  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In Western Desert, first supreme elder Tang Yang leads the Gu Immortals who gather after Tang Miao fails another exploration of Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable’s dream realm. The clan has explored the dream realm for sixty years and created a little more than a dozen dream realm mortal Gu, all rank three and below, with only a few suited to exploration. Among its many Gu Immortals, only Tang Fang Ming is treated as suited to this work: most of those mortal Gu are his, and he is the main force behind the clan’s dream realm exploration. He suffered a great loss and is still lost in the dream realm, and his sister Tang Miao keeps trying to pull him out. At this early stage Tang clan is already at the lead of the era, and even against Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects its progress is among the highest, though the era’s limits still leave it with that small mortal-Gu result.",
      "chapters": [
        775
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "western-desert-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_western_desert",
        "char_tang_yang",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_thieving_heaven_demon_venerable",
        "sys_mortal_gu",
        "fac_ten_great_ancient_sects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan names Steal Dream as Tang clan of Western Desert’s immortal killer move, a method that could steal a dream realm out of a grotto-heaven. In his previous life, Western Desert’s Tang clan had the deepest dream path foundation among the five regions. It had not been outstanding among the dozen or so Western Desert super forces, sitting at a middle to lower tier, then rose on dream path during the five regions chaotic war until it became Western Desert’s strongest force and a power that could stand tall among the five regions, in what Western Desert people called the Great Era of Tang.",
      "chapters": [
        776
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "previous-life-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "move_steal_dream",
        "evt_era_great"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "By the time Fang Yuan approaches it, Tang clan has declined to a mid-lower tier among Western Desert’s super forces, though it still holds an Immortal Gu House and, by its well-defended headquarters, a tributary of the River of Time that other forces cannot easily seize. Fang Yuan trades Shadow Sect’s dream path research for Tang clan opening that tributary as an escape route for him, along with the clan’s financial backing to produce guts Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1436
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "present-day-standing-and-the-river-of-time",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "loc_tributary_of_the_river_of_time",
        "fac_shadow_sect",
        "gu_guts_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The five regions chaotic war has not started, and the clan uncovered Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable’s dream realm earlier and has kept it secret while researching it. Tang clan is clueless about dream path and its progress is very slow, and what progress there is rests on Tang Fang Ming’s talent and ingenuity alone. He very nearly dies exploring it, and is saved only because his sister gives up her clues to Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable’s true inheritance in exchange for the help of White Sea Shatuo, a split soul of Spectral Soul Demon Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        1490
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tang-fang-mings-near-fatal-exploration",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
